CHANGES IN VERSION 1.21.1
-------------------------

    o The neighbour counts and edge corrections of lisa(), lisaClust() and inhomLocalK() are computed in C++
      (src/core, shared with the Python package lisaclust): about 8 to 18 times faster. The edge correction
      intersects each disc with the window exactly instead of through spatstat's integer-rounded polygon
      clipping, which changes the LISA by less than 1e-6; regions are otherwise unchanged.

    o hatchingPlot() and geom_hatching() are about 10 times faster: the hatching lines are intersected with the
      region outlines all at once, and the region of each grid point is that of the nearest cell, found in
      C++. Equidistant cells vote and a tied vote goes to the first region, so the plot no longer depends on the
      random seed.

    o Bug fix: lisaClust() assigned the regions to the wrong cells when the cells of different images were
      interleaved rather than ordered by image. Regions are now matched to cells by their position in the input.
      hatchingPlot() had the same problem with the region column, and now also accepts a data.frame.

    o Bug fix: regionMap() failed when a cell type had no cells (an unused factor level).

    o Bug fix: lisaClust() failed on a SpatialExperiment whose coordinates are only in spatialCoords().

    o lisaClust no longer depends on spicyR, simpleSeg, class, data.table or tidyr. The examples use simulated
      data, and the vignette finds tissue domains in triple-negative breast cancer and cellular niches in
      colorectal cancer, compared between groups of patients.
